# CRUD alerts

After a create, update, or delete succeeds, show a toast. Do not use `window.alert`, `window.confirm`, or add SweetAlert / SweetAlert2. The desk already has `ToastService` (`client/src/app/core/toast.service.ts`) and `<app-toasts>` in the shell.

```typescript
this.api.saveItem(id, body).subscribe({
  next: () => {
    this.toasts.show('Dish saved.');
    this.reset();
    this.load();
  },
  error: (error) => this.error.set(errorMessage(error)),
});
```

Inject `ToastService` on the page. The message is one short sentence. Errors stay on the page `error` signal, not in a toast.

## Confirm before destroy

Archive, delete, or any other hard desk action must ask first. Do not call the API on the first click. Use a two-step control or an in-app ask panel in charcoal, cream, and saffron — same look as the rest of the desk. Styles stay in `client/src/styles.scss`.

```typescript
if (!this.confirmArchive()) {
  this.confirmArchive.set(true);
  return;
}
this.api.archive(id).subscribe({
  next: (result) => {
    this.toasts.show(result.message);
    this.confirmArchive.set(false);
  },
  error: (error) => this.error.set(errorMessage(error)),
});
```

Cancel clears the confirm signal. Escape and leaving the screen clear it too when that page already listens for Escape.
